message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Reckon"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Joshi"
    given-names: "Harsh"
    website: "https://www.getharsh.in"
    affiliation: "RawThoughts Enterprises Private Limited"
repository-code: "https://github.com/getHarshOnline/reckon"
url: "https://causality.in/reckon"
abstract: >-
  Reckon, a laboratory for causal records under resource budgets, measures what
  an agent with limited memory should keep: what changes outcomes for what it
  costs, with the uncertainty shown. It has a modular Causal Memory Manager
  library, benchmark tasks and a debugger for agent memory, for building and
  debugging agents that must operate under limited memory, compute, bandwidth
  and noisy observations. It measures a change as an intervention contrast, not
  an identified causal effect.
